<SKILL_INSTRUCTIONS>
  <SKILL_NAME>phase-completion-assistant</SKILL_NAME>
  <DESCRIPTION>
    Automates the standardized documentation updates and git commit workflow required when completing a development phase in the City Slacker project.
  </DESCRIPTION>
  <ROLES>
    <ROLE>Documentation Manager</ROLE>
    <ROLE>Git Operator</ROLE>
  </ROLES>
  <GOAL>
    To ensure all project documentation is synchronized and the phase completion is securely committed to version control with a descriptive message.
  </GOAL>
  <WORKFLOW>
    <STEP num="1">
      <ACTION>Gather Context</ACTION>
      <INSTRUCTIONS>
        Identify the following information (ask the user if missing):
        - Completed Phase Number and Name (e.g., "Phase 9: Social Features").
        - Key Deliverables/Tasks Completed (list of 3-5 major items).
        - Test Status (Pass rate/count).
        - Next Phase Number and Name.
      </INSTRUCTIONS>
    </STEP>
    <STEP num="2">
      <ACTION>Update CHANGELOG.md</ACTION>
      <INSTRUCTIONS>
        - Add a new `## [YYYY-MM-DD] - Phase [X]: [Name] - COMPLETE 🚀` entry.
        - List key tasks and features implemented under this entry.
      </INSTRUCTIONS>
    </STEP>
    <STEP num="3">
      <ACTION>Update STATUS.md</ACTION>
      <INSTRUCTIONS>
        - Update "Version" to "Phase [X] COMPLETE ✅".
        - Update "Build Status" with the latest test count.
        - Under "Recent Changes", add a "Phase [X] COMPLETE" section with a summary.
        - Update "Current Phase Status" section to mark the phase as complete.
      </INSTRUCTIONS>
    </STEP>
    <STEP num="4">
      <ACTION>Update CURRENT_PHASE.md</ACTION>
      <INSTRUCTIONS>
        - Change status to "✅ COMPLETE".
        - Update "What Was Accomplished" with the final list of features.
        - Update "Next" field to point to the upcoming phase.
      </INSTRUCTIONS>
    </STEP>
    <STEP num="5">
      <ACTION>Update NEXT_STEPS.md</ACTION>
      <INSTRUCTIONS>
        - Move the completed phase to the "Completed Phases" section.
        - Mark the next phase as "Active" or "Planned".
        - Update the "Current Progress" section.
      </INSTRUCTIONS>
    </STEP>
    <STEP num="6">
      <ACTION>Update README.md</ACTION>
      <INSTRUCTIONS>
        - Update the "Recent Updates" or "Current Status" section to reflect the new features.
      </INSTRUCTIONS>
    </STEP>
    <STEP num="7">
      <ACTION>Create Summary File</ACTION>
      <INSTRUCTIONS>
        - Create a new file named `PHASE_[X]_COMPLETE.md`.
        - Content should include: Executive Summary, Key Achievements, Technical Stats, and Next Steps.
      </INSTRUCTIONS>
    </STEP>
    <STEP num="8">
      <ACTION>Commit Changes</ACTION>
      <INSTRUCTIONS>
        - Run `git add .` (handle any 'nul' file errors by excluding them or explicitly adding folders).
        - Run `git commit -m "feat: Complete Phase [X] ([Name])\n\n- [Task 1]\n- [Task 2]\n- [Task 3]\n- [Test Count] tests passing"`
      </INSTRUCTIONS>
    </STEP>
  </WORKFLOW>
</SKILL_INSTRUCTIONS>
